anthra_OSE
==========

anthra is the dark, anthracite skin family for text2skin, designed from 2010
to 2014 by Tomas Saxer on vdr-portal.de. anthra_OSE is his anthra_1920_OSE
(version 0.0.5) ported to text2skin 2.0; it keeps his design. It is the
floating sibling of anthra_FSE: menu and channel info keep a margin to the
edge of the screen. The original is at http://anthra.de/anthra-skins/.


Requirements
------------

text2skin >= 2.0 (skin format 1.2). An output device with true colour OSD
(e.g. softhddevice, vaapivideo); without it the skin falls back to 256 colours.
The font VDRSymbols Sans by Andreas Mair (Debian: vdrsymbols-ttf).


What is different from anthra_1920_OSE
--------------------------------------

- The skin has a new name, anthra_OSE. Both skins can be installed side by
  side, the options are set anew in the setup menu.
- No build options and no Make.config any more. The skin scales itself to the
  size of the OSD (designed for 1920x1080, tested on 1280x720, 1920x1080 and
  3840x2160); the options are set at runtime in the setup menu of text2skin.
- The lists of the menu logos are part of the skin file, anthra_conf is gone.
  They contain the entries of the original configuration, including those for
  the menu of yaVDR.
- EPG images and recording images come from a scraper plugin (tvscraper,
  scraper2vdr) instead of an image folder and a recording hook. With an image
  the title and the info line of a recording end before it.
- All windows use true colour.
- The video size is shown for UHD as well, the menu background without menu
  logos uses an image that exists, four names in the lists of the menu logos
  are corrected.


Options
-------

Setup -> Plugins -> text2skin -> "Options of skin 'anthra_OSE'":

  Channel logos                     left     (left, right, none)
  Path of the channel logos         /var/lib/vdr/channellogos
  Separator logos                   left     (left, right, none)
  Path of the separator logos       ../liquid-logos4separator
  Main menu logos                   yes
  Main menu font                    default  (default, small, large)
  Group lines in menus              center   (center, left)
  Timer info in the main menu       yes
  EPG images (scraper)              yes
  Recording images (scraper)        yes
  Signal display                    graph    (graph, digit)

Channel logos are looked up as <path>/<channel name>.png or
<path>/<channel ID>.png, separator logos as <path>/<name of the group
separator in channels.conf>.png. A relative path is taken from the folder of
the skin, ../liquid-logos4separator is therefore
<configdir>/plugins/text2skin/liquid-logos4separator. The logo boxes have the
format 16:9 (left 260x146, right 160x90 pixels).

The themes (Setup -> OSD -> Theme): darkamber, darkblue, darkorange, izeman,
lightamber, lightblue, lightgrey, lightmaroon, white, yabluedefault,
yabluelight.


Installation
------------

  make
  make install

The paths come from vdr.pc if available (skin: <configdir>/plugins/text2skin/
anthra_OSE, themes: <configdir>/themes, translations: <locdir>), otherwise
/var/lib/vdr and /usr/share/locale. DESTDIR is supported.

The skin file anthra_OSE.skin is put together from xml/*.xml.


Translations
------------

The texts of the skin come from Tomas Saxer's translations, Volume and Mute
from the VDR sources. The options are translated into German, Spanish,
Finnish, French, Italian and Dutch, the other languages show them in English.
